H0178.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 1 (apparently through the idea of prattling a father's name);
Meaning: properly, a mumble, i.e. a water-skin (from its hollow sound); hence a necromancer (ventriloquist, as from a jar)
KJV renders: bottle, familiar spirit.

H0179.strongs:
Origin: probably from 56; mournful;
Meaning: Obil, an Ishmaelite
KJV renders: Obil.

H0180.strongs:
Origin: or (shortened) אֻבָל ; from 2986 (in the sense of 2988);
Meaning: a stream
KJV renders: river.

H0181.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to rake together;
Meaning: a poker (for turning or gathering embers)
KJV renders: (fire-) brand.

H0182.strongs:
Origin: or (shortened) אֹדוֹת (only thus in the plural); from the same as 181;
Meaning: turnings (i.e. occasions); (adverb) on account of
KJV renders: (be-) cause, concerning, sake.

H0183.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to wish for
KJV renders: covet, (greatly) desire, be desirous, long, lust (after).

H0184.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to extend or mark out
KJV renders: point out.

H0185.strongs:
Origin: from 183;
Meaning: longing
KJV renders: desire, lust after, pleasure.

H0186.strongs:
Origin: perhaps by permutation for 5813, strong;
Meaning: Uzai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Uzai.

H0187.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Uzal, a son of Joktan
KJV renders: Uzal.

H0188.strongs:
Origin: probably from 183 (in the sense of crying out after);
Meaning: lamentation; also interjectionally Oh!
KJV renders: alas, woe.

H0189.strongs:
Origin: probably from 183; desirous;
Meaning: Evi, a Midianitish chief
KJV renders: Evi.

H0191.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (meaning to be perverse);
Meaning: (figuratively) silly
KJV renders: fool(-ish) (man).

H0192.strongs:
Origin: of Aramaic derivation and probably meaning soldier of Merodak;
Meaning: Evil-Merodak, a Babylonian king
KJV renders: Evil-merodach.

H0193.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to twist, i.e. (by implication) be strong;
Meaning: the body (as being rolled together); also powerful
KJV renders: mighty, strength.

H0194.strongs:
Origin: or (shortened) אֻלַי; from 176;
Meaning: if not; hence perhaps
KJV renders: if so be, may be, peradventure, unless.

H0195.strongs:
Origin: of Persian derivation;
Meaning: the Ulai (or Eulaeus), a river of Persia
KJV renders: Ulai.

H0196.strongs:
Origin: from 191;
Meaning: silly, foolish; hence (morally) impious
KJV renders: foolish.

H0197.strongs:
Origin: or (shortened), אֻלָם ; from 481 (in the sense of tying);
Meaning: a vestibule (as bound to the building)
KJV renders: porch.

H0198.strongs:
Origin: appar, from 481 (in the sense of dumbness); solitary;
Meaning: Ulam, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Ulam.

H0199.strongs:
Origin: apparently a variation of 194;
Meaning: however or on the contrary
KJV renders: as for, but, howbeit, in very deed, surely, truly, wherefore.
